custom.h: include a C runtime header before testing the runtime flavour on MinGW.

mingw-w64 defines _UCRT in _mingw.h, which every runtime header pulls in, when
the headers are configured for the Universal CRT (llvm-mingw and MSYS2's ucrt64
toolchains). config.h is awk.h's first include and ends by including custom.h,
whose MinGW section includes pc/mbc32.h; at that point no runtime header has
been seen, so both files take their msvcrt branches (mbstate32_t, gawk's own
mbrtoc32) while every later file, including pc/mbc32.c itself, takes the UCRT
branches, and the two halves no longer agree on types or names. Including
stdio.h first settles _UCRT before anything tests it; msvcrt builds see no
change.

--- custom.h
+++ custom.h
@@ -124,6 +124,9 @@
    config.h.  */
 #ifdef __MINGW32__
 #undef HAVE_UCHAR_H
+/* The C runtime flavour (_UCRT) is settled by the runtime headers, which nothing
+   has included yet when config.h ends here; pc/mbc32.h and this file test it.  */
+#include <stdio.h>
 #include "pc/mbc32.h"
 #include <wctype.h>
 #define towlower c32tolower
